{"id":"f3c5f400-a71f-4642-82e0-42ea15c23d68","article_key":"doi:10.1038/s41586-026-11007-3","title":"Reference genomes and fossils revise bat family phylogeny and biogeography","title_zh":"参考基因组与化石修正蝙蝠科系谱与生物地理学","doi":"10.1038/s41586-026-11007-3","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-026-11007-3","abstract":"Abstract Bats are extraordinary among mammals, having uniquely evolved powered flight and laryngeal echolocation, along with disease resistance, extended healthspans and the ability to hibernate 1 . However, the evolutionary history of bats and the understanding of these adaptations remain unresolved. We analysed chromosome-level, long-read genome assemblies from 103 bat species, including 42 new assemblies, representing all 21 bat families. This dataset, expanded in scope and assembly quality, yielded a new bat phylogeny. We placed Myzopodidae as the earliest branch within Vespertilionoidea, and resolved yangochiropteran relationships, identifying Emballonuroidea and Vespertilionoidea as sister groups. Our analysis revealed a mosaic evolutionary history across bats and explained why previous phylogenetic studies were misled. Chromosomal ancestral-state reconstructions supported 26 ancestral bat chromosomes. We integrated a morphological dataset of 699 characters for 65 species, including 44 pre-Quaternary fossils and representatives of most living bat families, with neutrally evolving genomic sites. Fossilized birth–death and dispersal–extinction cladogenesis analyses showed that bats, and thus powered flight, probably originated in Europe in the late Palaeocene, refuting African and North American origins. Placement of the fossil † Vielasia in the oldest ‘Eochiroptera’ clade indicates that laryngeal echolocation predates crown-bat diversification. Total evidence dating, including the fossil taxa, significantly reduced unrepresented basal branch lengths compared with molecular-only divergence estimates. By integrating comprehensive genomic and morphological datasets, analysed using innovative methods, we resolve long-standing controversies in bat biology and provide new insights into the evolutionary history and trait diversification of bats.","abstract_zh":"摘要 蝙蝠在哺乳动物中独具特色，拥有独特进化的有动力飞行和喉部回声定位，以及疾病抵抗、延长健康寿命和冬眠能力1。然而，蝙蝠的进化历史及其适应机制仍未得到充分阐明。我们分析了103种蝙蝠的染色体水平长读段基因组组装，其中包括42个新组装，涵盖了所有21个蝙蝠科。该数据集在范围和组装质量上均得到扩展，产生了新的蝙蝠系统发育树。我们将Myzopodidae定位为Vespertilionoidea内最早的分支，并解析了Yangochiropteran的关系，确定Emballonuroidea和Vespertilionoidea为姐妹群。我们的分析揭示了蝙蝠的多样化进化历史，并解释了为何先前的系统发育研究被误导。染色体祖先状态重建支持26条祖先蝙蝠染色体。我们整合了699个特征的形态学数据集，涵盖65个物种，包括44个第四纪前化石和大多数现存蝙蝠科的代表，并与中性进化的基因组位点相结合。化石化的出生–死亡和扩散–灭绝分支分析表明，蝙蝠及其有动力飞行可能起源于晚古近纪的欧洲，驳斥了非洲和北美的起源假说。将化石†Vielasia置于最古老的“Eochiroptera”分支中，表明喉部回声定位早于冠蝙蝠的多样化。包括化石分类的总证据定年显著缩短了与仅基于分子分歧估计相比未被代表的基底分支长度。通过整合全面的基因组和形态学数据集，并采用创新方法进行分析，我们解决了蝙蝠生物学中的长期争议，并为蝙蝠的进化历史和特征多样化提供了新的见解。","snippet":"Abstract Bats are extraordinary among mammals, having uniquely evolved powered flight and laryngeal echolocation, along with disease resistance, extended healthspans and the ability to hibernate 1 . However, the evolutionary history of bats and the understanding of these adaptations remain unresolved. We analysed chromosome-level, long-read genome assemblies from 103 bat species, including 42 new assemblies, represe…","translated_at":"2026-10-13T23:48:50.721961+00:00","translation_model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"journal-article","volume":"658","issue":"8134","published_at":"2026-09-23T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-10-13T21:20:30Z","display_date":"2026-10-13T21:20:30Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":"2026-09-23T00:00:00","print_published_at":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","first_author":"Ariadna E. Morales","authors_text":"Ariadna E. Morales, Yan Liang, William R. Thomas, Evgeny V. Leushkin, Francisco X. Castellanos, Denis M. Larkin, Tom Brown, Bastian Fromm, Suzanne J. Hand, Zixia Huang, Graham M. Hughes, Matthew F. Jones, Burton K. Lim, Meike Mai, Eugene W. Myers, Martin Pippel, Sebastien J. Puechma